## Schema Structure

The model follows a classic **star schema** pattern with one central fact table and three surrounding dimension tables.

### Fact Table — `Fact_Table`

The central table containing all measurable, quantitative data related to banking and crisis indicators.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| BANK | Text | Bank identifier |
| BANK_W3 | Numeric | Bank metric (weighted) |
| blanguar | Numeric | Financial measure |
| caplab | Numeric | Capital/labour indicator |
| CCC | Numeric | Financial index |
| contcrisis | Numeric | Crisis count measure |
| CrisisStatusKey | Foreign Key | Links to `Dim_CrisisStatus` |

> The fact table also holds foreign keys linking to `Dim_Country` and `Dim_Date`.

---

### Dimension Tables

#### `Dim_Country`
Provides geographic context for each record in the fact table.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Country_Key | Primary Key | Unique country identifier |

**Relationship:** `Dim_Country[Country_Key]` → `Fact_Table` (1-to-many)

---

#### `Dim_Date`
A dedicated date dimension table enabling time intelligence in DAX (YTD, MTD, QoQ, YoY).

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Date | Date | Full date value |
| Month | Numeric | Month number |
| Month Name | Text | Full month name |
| Quarter | Text | Quarter label (Q1–Q4) |
| Year | Numeric | Calendar year |

**Relationship:** `Dim_Date[Date]` → `Fact_Table` (1-to-many)

---

#### `Dim_CrisisStatus`
Classifies the type and status of financial/banking crises for categorical analysis.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| BANK | Text | Bank reference |
| contcrisis | Numeric | Crisis count |
| Index | Numeric | Crisis index |
| recession | Numeric | Recession indicator (binary) |
| RecessionAbroad | Numeric | Foreign recession indicator |
| TWIN | Numeric | Twin crisis indicator |

**Relationship:** `Fact_Table[CrisisStatusKey]` → `Dim_CrisisStatus` (many-to-1)

---

## Design Decisions

- **Star schema over snowflake:** Kept the model flat and denormalized for faster DAX performance and simpler measures.
- **Dedicated `Dim_Date` table:** Built as a proper calendar table to unlock all Power BI time intelligence functions without workarounds.
- **Proper cardinality:** All relationships are configured as many-to-one from the fact table to dimensions, with single-direction cross-filtering to avoid ambiguity.
- **Clean model view:** Tables arranged to reflect the star shape visually — fact table at the center, dimensions radiating outward — for clarity during review and presentation.

